            <div xml:id="d399">

                <pb facs="0791" n="779" sameAs="frus:frus1946v09/pg779"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/4–1746: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Mukden</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Clubb</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mukden</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-04-17T12:00:00+08:00">April 17,
                        1946—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 9:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>31. Am informed (ReConstel April 9, 9 a.m.<anchor n="15" xml:id="d399-f1"/>
                    penultimate paragraph) that Chinese on April 11 obtained control Fushun mine
                    from Soviets.</p>
                <p>Whether this recovery was unqualified is still unclear.</p>
                <p>Please repeat Chungking, Shanghai.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Clubb</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
